# The conformance cases of UAX #29's sentences for Unicode 17.0.0, run through `sentences`:
# every line of `SentenceBreakTest.txt` of https://www.unicode.org/Public/17.0.0/ucd/auxiliary/
# (SHA-256 12cb47d028ded0c1), each the code points of a text in hexadecimal between marks,
# `x` where the file allows no break and `/` where it writes one; the marks
# the file writes at the start and the end are left out, being the same on
# every line.
#
# Generated, never edited by hand: the Heroes program
# `rebel/generators/unicode_cases/` read the file, fetched 2026-11-22, and wrote
# this module whole; its `check` command says whether this module is still
# what it writes. Only a test build reads the cases.

use unicode/segment/internal/conform

# How many lines of the file the tests below run.
constant CASES: i64
    512

## Tests

